<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for May 7.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for May 7.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for UK gas consumption in the period May 5 to 7.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>May 5 (actual) 181 mcm, 42 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>May 6 (forecast) 238 mcm, 56 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>May 7 (forecast) 240 mcm, 56 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>May 5 (actual) 8.7 Celsius, SNT 11.8 Celsius</p>
<p>May 6 (forecast) 4.8 Celsius, SNT 11.9 Celsius</p>
<p>May 7 (forecast) 6.9 Celsius, SNT 12.0 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called for Tuesday, with none expected for Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
